// Strings: equality and length.
//
// NOTE: two string ops are eval-supported but not yet *type*-checked, so the
// strict front-end rejects them — parked until the typechecker catches up:
//   - `a ++ b` (Concat) has no String rule (BinaryOpMismatch), though eval
//     concatenates strings fine.
//   - `s.slice(start, end)` mismatches `slice(range: Range)` — eval takes two
//     args, the signature wants a Range (and `ExprKind::Range` isn't evaluated
//     yet either).

#[test]
fn equality() ( assert("hi" == "hi") )

#[test]
fn length() ( assert_eq("hello".len(), 5) )

#[test]
fn empty_length() ( assert_eq("".len(), 0) )
